From 77e60b268e0dc10679a4d3d5c8123d1122ee8f93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:39:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] RGB with no range given is full range

A picture carries its colour range as one bit, so a stream that does
not say is limited range. That is right for YCbCr and wrong for RGB,
which FFmpeg itself treats as full range: an addon decoder handing over
packed RGB with no range had it marked limited, and the software
renderer then expanded a picture that was full range already.

VideoPicture::IsFullRange() holds the rule, and the FFmpeg and addon
decoders both use it. A range that is given is used as before.

The addon decoder also translated the addon's format to an
AVPixelFormat four times for each picture, each logging a warning for a
format Kodi does not know. It does it once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
